  "racePreview": {
    "slug": "champ-antonelli-hits-brazil-as-mclaren-unleashes-upgrades-mw13dhbd",
    "round": 20,
    "raceSlug": "brazil",
    "title": "Sao Paulo GP",
    "season": "2026",
    "country": "Brazil",
    "flag": "br",
    "raceStart": "2026-11-08T17:00:00.000Z",
    "publishedAt": "2026-11-03",
    "headline": "Champ Antonelli Hits Brazil as McLaren Unleashes  Upgrades",
    "summary": "Kimi Antonelli arrives in Brazil as the F1 World Champion, while Mercedes chases the Constructors' title. McLaren brings major upgrades to the unpredictable Interlagos circuit.",
    "body": "Kimi Antonelli rolls into Sao Paulo as your new World Champion after locking up the title with a P3 in Mexico — pretty slick for the youngest champ ever, and he's even got a special Senna helmet for the occasion. Mercedes is looking to double down and clinch the Constructors' title here too, needing just three more points than Ferrari. Speaking of Ferrari, things got spicy in Mexico with Hamilton and Leclerc having a right old tangle and Fred Vasseur wasn't happy at all, calling it a \"lack of respect\" — not to mention George Russell bailing without a word to the media. Max Verstappen just snatched a win there, proving Red Bull are still seriously quick, bagging three of the last four victories.\n\nInterlagos is a proper old-school circuit, a real driver's track with those elevation changes, heavy braking, and technical bits – plus, the weather can turn on a dime, with rain forecast for pretty much every day, especially Sunday, which could make things wild. McLaren's desperate to claw back third from Red Bull in the Constructors' and they're chucking a load of upgrades at the car this weekend, including new front and rear wings, hoping to regain that edge. This circuit really tests car balance, traction, and how teams manage their electrical energy under these 2026 regulations, so keep an eye on who masters that.",
    "picks": {
      "winner": "Antonelli",
      "wildcard": "Norris"
    }
  },
